SDN-Based Network Utilization Monitor (Using POX)

OVERVIEW

This project implements a Software Defined Networking (SDN) based solution to monitor real-time bandwidth utilization across a network.
It uses the POX controller and Mininet emulator to collect port statistics and compute bandwidth dynamically.

---

PROBLEM STATEMENT 

To design and implement a system that:

* Collects byte counters from network switches
* Estimates bandwidth usage
* Displays utilization
* Updates periodically in real-time

---

ARCHITECTURE

The project follows the SDN architecture:

* Application Layer – Monitoring logic
* Control Layer – POX Controller
* Data Plane – OpenFlow switches (Mininet)

The controller communicates with switches using the OpenFlow protocol.

---
TOPOLOGY

* 3 Hosts: h1, h2, h3
* 1 Switch: s1
* Remote Controller: POX

---

TECHNOLOGIES USED

* Python
* POX Controller
* Mininet
* OpenFlow Protocol
* Linux (Ubuntu)

---

FEATURES

* Real-time bandwidth monitoring
* Periodic updates (every 5 seconds)
* Collects port statistics from switches
* Calculates bandwidth using byte counters
* Displays per-port utilization

---

WORKING PRINCIPLE

1. Controller sends Port Statistics Request

2. Switch responds with byte counters

3. Bandwidth is calculated using:

   Bandwidth (bps) = (Current Bytes − Previous Bytes) × 8 / Time Interval

4. Results are displayed per port

---

PROJECT STRUCTURE

```
SDN-Bandwidth-Monitor/
│
├── monitor.py        # POX controller module
├── run.sh            # Automation script
└── README.md
```

---

HOW TO RUN

1. Start POX Controller

```
cd pox
python3 pox.py forwarding.l2_learning monitor
```
 2. Run Mininet

```
sudo mn --topo single,3 --controller remote,ip=127.0.0.1,port=6633 --mac
```
3. Test the System

Ping test:

```
h1 ping -c 5 h2
```

High traffic test:

```
iperf h1 h2
```

---

SAMPLE OUTPUT

```
--- Switch 00-00-00-00-00-01 Bandwidth Report ---
Port | Rx (bps) | Tx (bps) | Total Bytes
1    | 1024.00  | 2048.00  | 123456
2    | 0.00     | 0.00     | 7890
3    | 0.00     | 0.00     | 7890

---

REQUIREMENTS

* Mininet installed
* POX controller setup
* Python 3

---

NOTES

* Place monitor.py inside pox/ext/ directory
* Ensure POX is running before starting Mininet

